/-!
# The universal property of blowing up

Stacks tag 0806 says that the blowup `b : X' ⟶ X` of a closed subscheme `Z ⊆ X` is a final
object of the category `C` of schemes `Y ⟶ X` on which the inverse image of `Z` is an effective
Cartier divisor. Its uniqueness half is proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/UniversalProperty.lean`. This file proves the
**existence** half — every object of `C` admits a morphism to the blowup over `X` — and hence
the tag, unconditionally.

The Stacks proof feeds the graded datum `ψ : ⨁ f^*ℐᵈ ⟶ ⨁ ℐ_Dᵈ` to the mapping-in half of the
universal property of relative `Proj` (Constructions, Section 01NS). That universal property is
not formalized in general, and this file does not formalize it in general either: what it proves
is the piece of it that the blowup needs, namely the mapping-in property **over an affine open of
the base**, where the relative `Proj` is an honest `Proj` of a graded ring and the datum `ψ` is
a ring map. Globally the construction is then local on the source, by the uniqueness half.

In detail, over an affine open `U` of the base the chart of the relative `Proj` of a situation
`s` is `Proj (s.sectionRingGrading U)` and
`Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.relativeProjChart_isPullback` identifies it with the part of the
relative `Proj` lying over `U`. So a morphism `W ⟶ Proj (s.sectionRingGrading U)` over `U`
yields a morphism `W ⟶ relativeProj s` over the base, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.fromOfGlobalSections` builds the former out of a ring map
`s.sectionRing U ⟶ Γ(W, ⊤)` whose irrelevant ideal generates. For the Rees algebra of a
quasi-coherent ideal `ℐ` that ring map is the division map of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/GradedDivide.lean`: a homogeneous section of degree `n`
is a section of `ℐⁿ`, hence divisible by `tⁿ` once the inverse image of `ℐ` on `W` is generated
by the single nonzerodivisor `t`, and dividing by `tⁿ` is exactly the degreewise description of
the source's `ψ`.

The two topological inputs the gluing needs are supplied by their tags: **Tag 02OS part (1)**,
that the blowup is an isomorphism over the complement of the centre, enters as the instance
`AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_blowUpToBase_restrict_compl_support`, and scheme-theoretic density of
the inverse image of that complement in each member of the cover is **Tag 07ZU** transported
along the open immersions of the cover by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_preimage_of_isOpenImmersion`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.RelativeProj.Situation.exists_hom_relativeProj_of_sectionRingHom`: **the mapping-in
  property of a relative `Proj` over an affine open of the base.** A ring map from the graded
  ring of local sections over `U` to the global sections of `W`, whose restriction to degree
  zero is the ring map of a morphism `W ⟶ U` and whose irrelevant ideal generates, defines a
  morphism `W ⟶ relativeProj s` over the base.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_hom_blowUp_of_ideal_eq_span`: the same for the blowup of a scheme in a
  quasi-coherent ideal sheaf, where the ring map is produced by division: if `W ⟶ U` is a
  morphism to an affine open of the base along which the centre pulls back to the principal
  ideal generated by a nonzerodivisor `t`, then `W` admits a morphism to the blowup over the
  base. This is unconditional.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_hom_blowUp_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor`: **the existence half of Tag
  0806 for the blowup of an arbitrary scheme in a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf.** Unconditional.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isTerminal_blowUp`: **Tag 0806.** The blowup is a final object of `C`.
  Unconditional; it supersedes `Stacks.Blowup.exists_nonempty_isTerminal_blowUp`, which is the
  same statement with two of its inputs as hypotheses.
* `Stacks.Blowup.ideal_map_specHomRingHom_resLE`: the inverse image of an ideal sheaf read on a
  pair of affine charts, in the spelling the chart construction uses.
* `Stacks.Blowup.exists_affineOpens_ideal_eq_span_le`: an effective Cartier divisor is cut out
  by a nonzerodivisor on arbitrarily small affine opens — Tag 01WS with the neighbourhood
  shrunk inside a prescribed open.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_comap_of_isOpenImmersion`: an effective Cartier
  divisor pulls back to one along an open immersion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Opens.isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_preimage_of_isOpenImmersion`:
  scheme-theoretic density passes to the inverse image along an open immersion.

## Implementation notes

The ring map of a morphism `w : W ⟶ U.toScheme` into an affine open is taken to be
`Stacks.Blowup.specHomRingHom (w ≫ hU.isoSpec.hom)`, because
`Stacks.Blowup.toSpecΓ_comp_specMap_specHomRingHom` recovers `w` from it with no further
hypothesis, which is what makes the compatibility of the chart morphism with the structure
morphism a two-line computation. `Stacks.Blowup.specHomRingHom_comp_isoSpec_hom` identifies it
with the composite of `Scheme.Opens.topIso` and `Scheme.Hom.appTop`, which is the spelling in
which the inverse-image ideal is computed.

`@[stacks 0806]` is attached to `Stacks.Blowup.isTerminal_blowUp`, which is the whole of the tag:
the blowup is an object of `C` and a final one. The intermediate statements are untagged, being
pieces of its proof rather than of the tag. The hypothesis-carrying
`Stacks.Blowup.exists_nonempty_isTerminal_blowUp` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/TerminalRelativeProj.lean` is now subsumed and has no
consumers; it is a candidate for deletion.

